---
kind: lore
id: term
title: The first morning of a term
---

// newTerm is raised once per run, before the day-1 slotStart. NG+ reads the
// term that just ended through prev.run.*.

<beat id="opening" on="newTerm" title="A new term">
  @headmistress{code="0010"}: Welcome to Lantern Academy. Ten days to the end of term. Keep your lanterns lit and your curfews kept.
</beat>

<beat id="recap" on="newTerm" title="Last term, remembered" priority="10" when="has(prev.run.route)">
  @you{code="0010" mono}: I have floated a lantern here before. Last term it was with {{prev.run.route}}. It ended with {{prev.run.ending}}.
  <match subject="prev.run.ending">
    <when is="good">
      @you{code="0020" mono}: It was a good ending. Why does it feel like I'm allowed another?
    </when>
    <when is="bittersweet">
      @you{code="0030" mono}: I let it go out. Not this time.
    </when>
    <when is="keeper">
      @you{code="0040" mono}: Somebody I will never meet again, and will never stop remembering.
    </when>
    <otherwise>
      @you{code="0050" mono}: I was on my own. The lake kept my secret.
    </otherwise>
  </match>
</beat>
